  "description": "UtcMilliTime for .NET 8.0 + .NET 10+ provides Unix time milliseconds (Int64) timestamps, similar to JavaScript's Date.now(), with cross-platform support and NTP synchronization. Features Task-based async APIs, async Main support, conversion extensions (ToIso8601String, ToUtcDateTime, etc.), and new chaining methods for timestamp manipulations (e.g., AddHours, SubtractDays).\n\n      Usage:\n      using UtcMilliTime;\n      ITime time = Clock.Time;\n      time.SuppressNetworkCalls = false; // Enable NTP sync\n      var timestamp = time.Now; // Int64 timestamp\n      string iso = timestamp.ToIso8601String(); // ISO-8601 string\n\n      For async Main:\n      await Clock.CreateAsync();\n\n      See https://github.com/JPKusumi/UtcMilliTime for details.",
  "id": "UtcMilliTime",
